# The "fake" profile keeps the production auth topology but replaces GitHub with the disposable
# fake IdP. Ordinary web, oracle, and spawnctl clients still obtain AS-issued paired credentials.

# --- fake GitHub IdP (AS stubs the GitHub login; not dev-gated, valid with SPAWNERY_ENV=prod) ---
AS_FAKE_GITHUB=1
AS_FAKE_GITHUB_ADDR=0.0.0.0:9099
AS_FAKE_GITHUB_BASE_URL=http://@@HOST@@:9099
AS_FAKE_GITHUB_USERS=acc-owner-1,acc-owner-2,acc-owner-3
AS_MAX_FAMILIES=100
AS_DEVICE_PER_MIN=100

# The node runs the github static-token lane (local Gitea; see gitea.env), where github: mounts use
# one node-static token, not a per-owner AS mint. So the CreateSpawn owner-github-link preflight is
# meaningless here and would wrongly reject — disable it. (github_link_preflight_test.go still covers
# the preflight logic hermetically.)
#
# Still true after sp-wwtc's mint wiring (AS_URL, common.env): that wires cfg.GitHubMint != nil on the
# node, which switches ON the per-spawn MITM CA / HTTP_PROXY plumbing (internal/node/attach.go,
# GitHubControlEnabled) for every github: mount — but GITHUB_STATIC_TOKEN (gitea.env) staying set means
# mintGitHubMountsAtProvision still returns early (GitHubStaticCredentialsEnabled short-circuits it),
# so the actual git credential is still the node-static Gitea PAT, never a per-owner AS mint. No
# Fake OAuth acceptance identity (acc-owner-1/2/3) has an AS github-link on this stack — nothing in
# acceptance/ drives the AS OAuth link flow — so flipping GITHUB_STATIC_TOKEN off and re-enabling this
# preflight would reject every github: mount create outright. That's a real follow-up (exercise the
# AS-mint credential path end-to-end, not just the MITM CA/proxy plumbing) but needs an acceptance-side
# link step first; out of scope here.
CP_GITHUB_LINK_PREFLIGHT_DISABLED=1

# --- sidecar upstream CA trust override (sp-wwtc.3, e2e/VM profile ONLY) ---
# Merged bundle (system roots + the golden CA; built at provision time — see provision.sh) mounted
# into the sidecar with SSL_CERT_FILE pointed at it, so the sidecar's STRICT, UNMODIFIED upstream
# transport (newDefaultUpstreamTransport — no InsecureSkipVerify) genuinely verifies Gitea's
# github.com cert (sp-wwtc.1) against the golden CA. Production leaves this unset: no mount, no
# env override, no golden CA anywhere near the production sidecar image.
SIDECAR_CA_BUNDLE_FILE=/etc/spawnery/sidecar-ca-bundle/ca-bundle.crt
